# Anti Miscount Concern

## Scope
Prevent stock count drift by using CMS as single source of truth - all stock operations go through CMS with atomic increments/decrements, no local caching of stock values.

## Out of Scope
Complex reconciliation processes, manual stock adjustment workflows, distributed stock aggregation beyond CMS.

# Aftermath target
After completion: CMS as single source of truth for stock, all stock operations atomic in CMS, no local stock caching, stock count always accurate. No drift between actual and reported stock.

## Definition of Done
[ ] Single source of truth: CMS is only stock storage
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Stock fetch from CMS', { productId, stock })` when reading stock
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Stock update in CMS', { productId, delta })` when updating stock
    [ ] Test: All stock reads go to CMS, no local cache
[ ] Atomic operations: stock changes atomic in CMS
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Atomic stock increment', { productId, delta, newStock })` on increment
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Atomic stock decrement', { productId, delta, newStock })` on decrement
    [ ] Test: Concurrent stock updates, verify no drift
[ ] No local caching: never cache stock locally
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Stock cache check', { hasLocalCache: false })` on every stock operation
    [ ] Test: Verify no local stock variables in code
